## Self-exclusion statement

**Zero verified public benchmark numbers** found for Nemotron 3.5 Bolt E4B / `opencode/nemotron-3.5-bolt-e4b`.

The model does not have benchmark entries on BenchLM (0/639), has a gated/inaccessible HuggingFace page (401), and is absent from Artificial Analysis (403) and NGC (404). While the sibling 74B-A9B variant has published benchmarks, the E4B (4-bit) variant itself has no public benchmark data. Per the self-exclusion rule, scores from a different model variant cannot be used.

Per `RULES.md` §[Self-exclusion]: "if you found ZERO verified public benchmark numbers for this exact model/ID → refuse to score, write `Laguna_S_2.1.md.excluded` instead, and stop — do not fabricate or guess."

This model is therefore **self-excluded** from scoring. When Nemotron 3.5 Bolt E4B publishes benchmark numbers on BenchLM, Artificial Analysis, or an official NVIDIA announcement, this file should be replaced with a scored `Laguna_S_2.1.md`.

